Description: QR code and barcode scanner for Linux desktop
 A missing native QR Code scanner application for Linux desktop.
 .
 CoBang decodes QR codes and barcodes from a webcam or from a still image,
 and presents structured payloads such as URLs, Wi-Fi credentials and plain
 text in a readable way. It can also generate QR codes from text or from a
 Wi-Fi network picked from NetworkManager.
 .
 To be part of Linux desktop modernization, it is set to support Wayland
 (not XWayland), and only implements a native GUI (no web crap).
